# ai-i18n-tools — project rule

## Stack and purpose

TypeScript (strict), ESM, Node ≥ 22.16, pnpm ≥ 11.0; build `tsc`, test Vitest, lint ESLint + Prettier. CLI + library: **UI strings** (`t("…")` → catalog → locales) and **document translation** (markdown/mdx/JSON → SQLite cache → outputs). Config: `ai-i18n-tools.config.json`; runtime: `ai-i18n-tools/runtime`.

## Layout

Source `src/` (API from `src/index.ts`), tests `tests/`. Main areas: `cli/`, `core/`, `extractors/`, `processors/`, `api/`, `glossary/`, `runtime/`, `server/`, `utils/`. CLI entry: `dist/cli/index.js` (`package.json` `"bin"`).

## Required context before code changes

Before modifying **any** source, tests, examples, or config in this repo, read and apply [`docs/ai-i18n-tools-context.md`](docs/ai-i18n-tools-context.md) — especially **UI strings: catalog vs flat bundles** (English source text is the key in `public/locales/*.json`; `strings.json` is the extraction cache with MD5-8 ids, not the runtime bundle). Do not implement runtime `t()` lookup by hash unless you are working inside `ai-i18n-tools/runtime` itself.

## Docs

- Canonical package docs: `README.md`, `docs/`. Maintainer internals: `dev/package-context.md`. Consumer-facing shipped doc: `docs/ai-i18n-tools-context.md` (required reading for agents; see above).
- Treat `translated-docs/` as pipeline output from `translate-docs` (do not hand-edit unless you intend to refresh generated artifacts). Avoid bold around inline code in prose (translation tooling).
- Do **not** use bold formatting around inline code—avoid putting asterisks outside a backtick span. Use plain `` `code` `` spans, or apply emphasis and code styling separately; never nest both on the same element.
- Do **not** use bold formatting around links—avoid putting asterisks outside a link. Use plain `` [link text](url) `` spans, or apply emphasis and link styling separately; never nest both on the same element. If needed a bold use it inside the link text.


## How to work

Prefer repo search over guessing. For entrypoints and scripts, read `package.json` and the files you touch—do not assume paths like `src/main/`.

## CHANGELOG — required with behavioral changes

**Whenever you change behavior, fix bugs, change config/schema, or touch dependencies**, finish the task by adding at least one bullet under `## [Unreleased]` in `dev/CHANGELOG.md` in the **same edit session** as the code—not as a follow-up.

**Skip a CHANGELOG bullet only** when the change is documentation-only, comments-only, or otherwise has no user-visible or maintainer-relevant effect.

Match existing Unreleased lines: `- **{Type}**: {scope} - …` where Type is Added, Changed, Deprecated, Removed, Fixed, or Security; scope is a short subsystem name; description is one or two clear sentences (backticks for identifiers and paths). One bullet per logical change.

## Code habits

Prefer `async/await`; no empty catches. Validate config and external shapes with Zod. Tests: Vitest `describe`/`it`. Verify with `pnpm test` / `pnpm lint` when you change code.
